p.src:
The reason sines and cosines solve the equation is immediate: $\begin{aligned}
 \frac{d^2}{dt^2}\cos\omega t&=-\omega^2\cos\omega t,\\
 \frac{d^2}{dt^2}\sin\omega t&=-\omega^2\sin\omega t.\end{aligned}$ The general real solution is $x(t)=A\cos\omega t+B\sin\omega t.$

