 \end{aligned}

p.src:
One technical condition is already unavoidable. To replace velocities by momenta, the relations $p_i=\frac{\partial\mathcal L}{\partial\dot q_i}$ must be invertible for $\dot q_i(q,p)$. For an ordinary unconstrained system, local invertibility requires $\det\left(
 \frac{\partial^2\mathcal L}
 {\partial\dot q_i\,\partial\dot q_j}
 \right)\ne0.$

